[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139764,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Angiosarcoma of bone (AS-B) is a highly aggressive sarcoma with endothelial differentiation. It is extremely rare in the orbit.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139765,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9120/3 Angiosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139766,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B56.Y &amp; XH6264 Angiosarcoma, other specified primary site &amp; Haemangiosarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139767,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139768,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139769,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The orbit and adjacent cranial structures can be affected, with extension into the cranium, organs, and external soft tissue {9932897}. AS-B can be multifocal {34742485}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139770,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AS-B usually presents as a rapidly growing mass with symptoms depending on the site, including visual disorders (e.g. diplopia), exophthalmia, chemosis, ptosis, and pain/headache {9932897}.</p>\r\n<p>Radiographically, AS-B appears lytic and aggressive with poorly defined borders and frequent cortical destruction with extraosseous spread {34742485}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139771,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AS-B is rare (&lt;&nbsp;1% of malignant bone tumours) with the orbit one of the least frequent sites {34742485;9932897}. Primary AS from other sites exceptionally metastasizes to the orbit {21165236}. AS-B typically affects elderly people {34742485}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139772,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is mostly unknown, but radiation therapy can be causative {17998731;9932897}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139773,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The pathogenesis is complex with karyotypic and genetic heterogeneity with overlap with AS at other sites. <em>MYC</em> amplification is not necessarily associated with previous radiation therapy {34742485;25231439}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139774,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AS-B is typically haemorrhagic, friable, and destructive, with poorly defined borders and commonly extraosseous extension {34742485}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139775,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Primary AS-Bs usually show epithelioid morphology with a diffuse and permeative growth pattern. Spindle cell tumours are less frequent, and in this case metastasis from elsewhere needs to be ruled out {34742485;21323951}.</p>\r\n<p>Appearances range from relatively well to poorly formed vascular channels with variable solid growth and heterogeneity within a single neoplasm. Atypical (mainly epithelioid) endothelial cells show enlarged often hyperchromatic nuclei and frequently distinct nucleoli. Mitoses, haemorrhage, and necrosis are more frequent in less-differentiated tumours.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>AS expresses CD31, ERG, and FLI1. There is often variable cytokeratin expression in tumours with epithelioid morphology, which can lead to confusion with metastatic carcinoma {34742485;31950476;21323951}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>This includes metastatic carcinoma, epithelioid haemangioendothelioma, pseudomyogenic (epithelioid sarcoma&ndash;like) haemangioendothelioma, epithelioid haemangioma, Kaposi sarcoma, and melanoma {34742485}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139776,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139777,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139778,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> bone as primary site; microscopically, at least focally, vasoformative appearance and/or immunohistochemical expression of endothelial markers; prominent nuclear atypia and readily observed mitoses.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139779,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) and American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) TNM8 staging system for soft tissue sarcoma of the trunk and extremities is used.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139780,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 299,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The prognosis is very poor, and site and stage dependent {34742485}, with general 5-year overall survival for skeletal AS &lt;&nbsp;40%. Cases may be managed by surgery, chemotherapy, radiotherapy, or a combination thereof {34742485}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:08:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]